\includegraphics{fig_decoder}
\caption{\normalsize Left: a strongly connected partial 6-state binary DFA;
right: the literal automaton of the prefix code $\{abaaa,abaab,abab,abba\}$.}
\label{fig:examples}
\end{figure}

An example of a strongly connected partial DFA is shown in~\Cref{fig:examples} (left).
We have two undefined transitions: $\delta(q_3,b)=\delta(q_6,b)=\bot$.
The unique shortest reset word is $bab$: $\delta(Q,b)=\{q_1,q_2,q_5\}$, $\delta(Q,ba)=\{q_2,q_3,q_6\}$, and $\delta(Q,bab) = \{q_2\}$.
However, in contrast with the case of a complete DFA, the preimage $\delta^{-1}(\{q_2\},bab) = \{q_1,q_4\}$ is not $Q$.

